. The recent days show Ford averaging about 2.3 naps/day with short naps (~51 min average). On March 30, a 3-nap day with 2h20m total nap preceded a harder night (score <50), while the data doesn''t show clear best-night examples, so I''ll aim for the parent''s 2-nap target with a moderate total daytime sleep (~2.5-3h) to avoid oversleeping during the day which could worsen night fragmentation.

