 is above his average, so we need one more nap to round out the day on a 2-nap schedule.

Ford has been awake since 1:18 PM, making it 2h 42m of wake time right now. At 7 months this is a reasonable second wake window — not too short, not overly stretched. His historical wake windows often run longer (3h+), but many of those preceded harder nights, so I''m comfortable recommending a nap right at ~2h 42m (162 min). I''m capping this nap at 40 minutes to keep total daytime sleep around 1h 40m, which is moderate and leaves enough sleep pressure for bedtime. His remaining budget is ~1h 57m, but given that his best nights don''t seem to follow very high daytime sleep totals, a cap of 40 minutes (total day ~1h 43m) is appropriate.

