t was particularly rough with only about 11h15m of broken night sleep. Today he got a solid 1h3m first nap, which is above his average — a good sign. He''s now been awake 2h41m, which is right in the age-appropriate range (2h15m–3h) and close to his shorter observed wake windows.

I''m recommending Nap 2 start now at 4:00 PM with a 40-minute cap. The wake window of ~162 minutes (2h42m) is appropriate — not too short, not too long — especially given his rough night. I''m capping at 40 minutes rather than letting him sleep longer because: (1) he only has about 1h57m of nap budget remaining, but we need to protect bedtime timing, and (2) a 35-40 minute nap ending around 4:35-4:40 PM leaves a solid last wake window of about 1h50m-2h before the parent''s earliest acceptable bedtime of 6:30 PM. Given his age and overtiredness from last night, a slightly shorter last wake window is appropriate.

