r 0 naps / 0 min. This suggests a 2-nap day with moderate total daytime sleep (~2h) is a reasonable target. Yesterday''s 2-nap schedule (1h 3m + 27m = 1h 30m total) led to a night with a decent first stretch of 7h 11m, so aiming for slightly more total nap (~2h) should be fine.

For the wake window before Nap 2, I''m recommending 2h 45m (165 min). While Ford''s observed average is 3h 30m, that average is inflated by some very long windows that likely contributed to overtiredness and poor nights. At 7 months, the age-appropriate range is 2h 15m–3h, and Ford has had a fragmented night (total night sleep was roughly 10h but broken into multiple segments with wake-ups at 2:51 AM, 5:48 AM, and 6:13 AM). A 2h 45m window balances Ford''s tendency to run a bit longer than textbook while not pushing into overtired territory. This lands Nap 2 at 3:05 PM.

For the rest-of-day plan: Nap 2 starts at 3:05 PM, capped at 60 minutes (to keep total daytime nap at ~2h, which is within the 3h budget and aligns with the moderate total nap that preceded better nights). If Ford sleeps the expected 45 min, wake-up is around 3:50 PM. With a last wake window of about 2h 45m–3h, bedtime lands at approximately 6:45 PM, which respects the parent''s earliest bedtime preference of 6:30 PM. If Ford sleeps the full 60-minute cap, wake at 4:05 PM and bedtime at ~6:50–7:00 PM, which is also excellent.', '2026-04-02 18:17:46.587137+00', '7181e3f8-2207-43be-894c-ddfd0e3271ae'),
	('08a3dd1c-213c-4343-a6fd-d8a79275fcd3', 'next_nap', '2026-04-02 19:15:00+00', '2026-04-02 19:30:00+00', 75, '2026-04-02 23:30:00+00', 177, '08a3dd1c-213c-4343-a6fd-d8a79275fcd3:e25e2d70-d276-4a37-b439-cf2ed0e7fe61:2026-04-02T16:17:52+00:00|7403d782-5dec-45f9-8dad-eb0853a2cca7:2026-04-02T11:35:00+00:00|61dd0b63-fdca-4a6f-883d-cda17b5bbc8f:2026-04-02T10:48:00+00:00|000eaf46-2c07-4f7a-a353-7fea0c72cb8b:2026-04-02T07:51:00+00:00|c837a428-1621-4a29-9c08-15735c38bd40:2026-04-01T21:40:00+00:00|1c896e8c-80da-448f-a172-6b9acbc697b9:2026-04-01T18:18:00+00:00|bad84c7b-fd70-4623-8d31-7eefec220811:2026-04-01T11:42:00+00:00|990a992a-e04c-4b67-acd1-c0cb7acc021b:2026-04-01T10:06:18.873+00:00|bd358c28-ecb2-4879-aef5-2bab224659c6:2026-04-01T07:44:02.553+00:00|ef4a2c9e-030c-4e2d-b8a3-0d15006ff61a:2026-04-01T03:32:00+00:00:Earliest bedtime the parent wants is 6:30 PM.', '[{"note": "Cap at 75 min to protect nap budget and night sleep", "time": "2:15 PM", "event": "nap_start", "label": "Nap 2 start", "cap_minutes": 75, "wake_window_minutes": 178}, {"time": "3:00 PM", "event": "nap_end", "label": "Nap 2 end (expected ~45 min; wake by 3:30 PM at latest)"}, {"note": "Adjust to ~7:00 PM if nap runs to the 75-min cap (3:30 PM wake)", "time": "6:30 PM", "event": "bedtime", "label": "Bedtime", "wake_window_minutes": 180}]', 'Ford''s first nap was a great 1h 42m, so Nap 2 should be capped to keep total daytime sleep around 2.5–3h. A wake window of ~3h after Nap 1 sets up a solid last wake window before a 6:30 PM bedtime.', 'Ford is 7 months old and averaging 2 naps/day, which aligns with the parent''s target of 2 naps. His observed wake windows average around 3h 21m, though some stretch much longer (up to 5h 33m). His age-typical range is 2h 15m–3h, but this baby clearly runs longer than textbook — his recent data shows wake windows consistently around 3h or more. Today''s first nap was excellent at 1h 42m (starting 9:35 AM, ending 11:17 AM), which is well above his average of 49 min. This means the remaining nap budget is about 1h 18m to stay within a ~3h total day nap goal.

The harder nights (score <50) followed days with either 3 naps and ~2h 20m total nap, or 0 naps. The best approach is to stick with 2 naps and aim for total daytime sleep around 2.5–3h. With 1h 42m already banked, Nap 2 should be capped at 75 minutes (the remaining budget of ~1h 18m, rounded to nearest 5). I expect Ford will likely sleep around 45 minutes based on his typical nap lengths for a second nap, but the 75-minute cap gives room if he sleeps longer while still protecting night sleep. The wake window from Nap 1 end (11:17 AM) to Nap 2 start (2:15 PM) is about 2h 58m, which fits well within Ford''s demonstrated patterns — he regularly does 3h windows and this is his mid-day window where a slightly shorter stretch is appropriate given the strong first nap.

For the rest of the day: Nap 2 starts at 2:15 PM, and if Ford sleeps ~45 min he''d wake around 3:00 PM. With a last wake window of about 3h 30m (consistent with his longer last wake windows seen in the data — e.g., his 4:40 PM nap end to 7:40 PM bedtime was 3h), bedtime would land around 6:30 PM, which matches the parent''s earliest bedtime preference perfectly. If he sleeps the full 75-minute cap, he''d wake at 3:30 PM and bedtime would shift to ~7:00 PM, which is also excellent. Either way, the schedule supports good night sleep.', '2026-04-02 18:20:46.952074+00', 'a23028ab-1c37-4548-b28a-1b7681c7e9c4'),
