ed to manage the remaining nap budget carefully. The remaining nap budget is about 1h 18m to stay within the ~3h total day target. The harder nights in the data followed days with 3 naps or 0 naps and higher/lower total nap amounts, so sticking with 2 naps and a moderate total (around 2h 15m–2h 45m) seems ideal.

For the wake window before Nap 2, I''m recommending approximately 3 hours (178 minutes) after Nap 1 ended at 11:17 AM, placing Nap 2 start at 2:15 PM. This is within Ford''s demonstrated range and slightly below his average observed wake window, which makes sense as a mid-day window (his longest windows tend to be the last one before bed). I''m capping Nap 2 at 75 minutes — this is the maximum, not the expected duration. His typical nap is ~45 min, but if he sleeps longer we want to wake him by 75 min to keep total day nap around 2h 57m (within budget) and to preserve enough sleep pressure for bedtime. Realistically he''ll likely sleep 30–50 minutes based on his patterns for second naps.

