orning nap, and we''ll plan a 2-nap day to protect tonight''s sleep.', 'Looking at Ford''s data, his nights have been very fragmented — last night he got roughly 10.5 hours of night sleep but broken into multiple chunks (6:35 PM–8:46 PM, 8:42 PM–11:10 PM, 11:38 PM–5:38 AM). His best night recently (Apr 1, 7:40 PM–2:51 AM = 7h 11m unbroken) followed a 2-nap day with about 1h 30m total daytime sleep. Days with only 1 nap and very little daytime sleep led to harder nights. This tells me Ford needs a solid 2-nap day with adequate total daytime sleep (around 2–2.5 hours) to set up a better night.

