 3h 38m) totaling roughly 9h 39m of night sleep spread across many segments. This is a rough night, so Ford is likely carrying a sleep debt. His recent pattern shows 2 naps per day, which aligns with the parent''s target. On April 2, his best day structure was a longer first nap (1h 42m) and a shorter second nap (31m), totaling about 2h 13m of daytime sleep. On April 1, it was 1h 3m + 27m = 1h 30m. The harder nights followed days with lower total nap minutes (~1h 30m or less), so aiming for more total daytime sleep (~2h to 2h 30m) seems beneficial.

