For the rest of the day: If Nap 2 runs about 60 minutes (ending ~2:00 PM), that leaves a last wake window of about 4h 30m to a 6:30 PM bedtime — that''s too long. If Nap 2 runs the full cap of 1h 55m (ending ~2:55 PM), the last wake window to 6:30 PM bedtime would be about 3h 35m, which is on the longer side but within Ford''s demonstrated range (he''s done 3h 31m recently). Given the parent is open to a slightly later bedtime, if the nap runs shorter (say ~60 min ending at 2:00 PM), we''d target bedtime around 5:00–5:30 PM which is too early. So ideally Ford sleeps closer to the cap. I''ll plan for a realistic scenario: nap ends around 2:55 PM with the cap, bedtime at 6:30 PM with a ~3h 35m last wake window. If the nap is shorter, the parent can adjust bedtime earlier (but not before 6:00 PM).', '2026-04-06 15:25:48.864477+00', '6483cc37-0bea-4473-9b07-d7f79912a822'),
